# Data Models Reference

Source of truth: `app/models.py`. Read it directly when in doubt — never trust docs over the actual model.

## Model Hierarchy

```
Subject (id: string, e.g. 'MATC')
  └── Topic (subject_id, sort_order)
        └── Subtopic (topic_id, hidden, sort_order)

Chapter (subject_id, sort_order)
  └── Subchapter (chapter_id, hidden, sort_order)

Question (qid, subject, source, year, paper, section, qno, q_type, level, ...)
  ├── major_topic_id → Topic
  ├── major_subtopic_id → Subtopic  (must belong to major_topic)
  ├── minor_topics → [Topic]  (M2M via question_minor_topics)
  ├── subtopics → [Subtopic]  (M2M via question_subtopics)
  ├── chapter_id → Chapter
  ├── subchapter_id → Subchapter
  └── assets → [QuestionAsset]

QuestionAsset (question_id, asset_type, file_format, language, file_path, part_number)

User (username, password_hash, is_super_admin)
  └── subject_permissions → [UserSubjectPermission]

UserSubjectPermission (user_id, subject_id, role)  — role: 'viewer'|'user'|'admin'
SavedFilter (user_id, name, filter_data JSON, is_starred, is_shared)
SavedGenerationProfile (user_id, name, options_data JSON, is_starred, is_shared, created_at, updated_at)
FileSection (user_id, name, sort_order, sort_field, sort_direction, page_size, collapsed, is_default)
GeneratedFile (user_id, display_name, filename, status, filter_data, generation_options JSON, section_id, manual_position, ...)
FileShare (file_id?, section_id?, shared_by_user_id, shared_with_user_id)  — XOR(file_id, section_id)
SystemSetting (key PK, value Text/JSON, updated_at, updated_by FK)
```

## Key Question Fields
| Field | Notes |
|---|---|
| `qid` | Unique string ID, indexed. Format: `MATC_DSE_2024_P1_Q5` |
| `source` | `DSE`, `CE`, `AL`, `QB` |
| `q_type` | `MC`, `CQ`, or NULL (auto-set by ingestor for MATC only) |
| `level` | 1–3 or NULL (manually tagged) |
| `section` | Free text (e.g. `A`, `Section I`) |
| `correct_percentage` | 0–100 or NULL (public exam correct rate) |
| `answer` | Text answer (alternative to ANS image) |
| `comment` | Notes/commentary text |

## QuestionAsset Constraints
- `asset_type`: `QUE`, `ANS`, `SOL`
- `file_format`: `IMG`, `DOC`, `MD`
  - `MD` is single-part only (one `.md` = one whole asset, self-contained with LaTeX math + base64 images). Ingest skips any `.md` with `part_number > 1`; upload rejects a second MD for the same `(question, asset_type, language)` slot.
- `language`: `EN`, `CH`, `BI`
- `part_number`: int starting at 1 (for multi-image questions; always 1 for MD)
- Unique constraint: `(question_id, asset_type, language, file_format, part_number)`
- `file_path` stored as forward-slash relative path from `SOURCE_PATH`

## Permission Checks (User model methods)
- `user.has_subject_access(subject_id)` — any access (viewer/user/admin)
- `user.is_subject_admin(subject_id)` — admin role or super admin
- `user.can_generate()` — has 'user' or 'admin' role for ANY subject
- `user.is_all_view_only()` — all permissions are 'viewer'
- `user.get_subject_roles()` → `{subject_id: role}`

## GeneratedFile Status Flow
`pending` → `generating` → `completed` | `failed`

Stale `pending`/`generating` records are reset to `failed` on app startup (in `create_app()`).

## My Files Sections & Sharing
- `FileSection` is the per-user folder model for the My Files page. Each user has exactly one row with `is_default=True` (the "Latest" inbox) — auto-created lazily via `_get_or_create_default_section` in `app/user.py` on first /user/files load and whenever the generator creates a new `GeneratedFile`.
- `GeneratedFile.section_id` is nullable + ON DELETE SET NULL. New files always land in the owner's default section. Section deletion moves contained files back to default; nothing is ever orphaned.
- `FileShare` records a per-target-user share. Exactly one of (`file_id`, `section_id`) is non-NULL (DB CHECK constraint). Sharing a section transitively shares every file in it (resolution at query time, not materialised).
- Visibility helper: `_user_can_view_file(gf, user)` returns True if user owns the file, is super-admin, OR has any `FileShare` row matching `(file_id=gf OR section_id=gf.section_id)`.
- Mutation helper: `_user_owns_file(gf, user)` — only the owner / super-admin can move / rename / delete. Sharing controls (toggle / list) are super-admin-only.
- See [user-files-profiles.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/user-files-profiles.mdc) for the full API + frontend layout.

## SystemSetting (DB-backed runtime config)
Key/value table that overrides `.env` / `Config` bootstrap defaults at runtime. The full registry of tunables (type/label/help/validator) lives in `app/settings.py`. See [system-settings.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/system-settings.mdc) for the precedence rules, hot-reload semantics, and "adding a new tunable" guide.

The table is auto-created on app startup if missing — no manual migration step needed when upgrading.
